---
id: org.dxos.plugin.cloudflareOs
name: CloudflareOsPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Uses a [Cloudflare OS](https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflare-os) deployment as a backend for a
Composer space. Composer stays the frontend and ECHO stays the system of record; the deployment
supplies three things Composer does not have: gadgets (per-user apps that run in a sandbox), an agent
that builds and changes them, and gatekeepers that let that agent act on outside services only with
the user's approval.

The plugin talks to the deployment over Cap'n Web, against the subset of the Workshop API that
`Protocol` declares. The workspace article holds a live session over a WebSocket at `/api`, as the
Workshop frontend does; an agent turn follows its workspace chat by polling with one-request HTTP
batches. That API is unversioned and moves with each deployment, so the subset is kept small.

