## Types

```mdl
type Workspace
  desc: |
    The Cloudflare OS workspace a space is bound to. The space holds one; it is the sync target
    of a Cloudflare OS connection. Gadgets and workspace chats stay on the deployment; this object
    names the workspace and lists its gadgets as of the last sync.
  fields:
    name?: string
    workspaceId: string          # the workspace id on the deployment
    connection: Ref<Connection>  # the account and deployment the workspace lives on
    gadgets?: Gadget[]
```

```mdl
type Gadget
  desc: A gadget of the workspace, as of the last sync.
  fields:
    id: number                   # the gadget's workpiece id in its workspace
    title: string
    chatId?: number              # set while the gadget exists only in that chat's proposed changes
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Connect a Cloudflare OS account

  req F-1.1: The connector form takes the deployment URL, a username and a password, and stores
    only the session token `login()` returns, never the password.
  req F-1.2: The password is hashed in the client with argon2id, salted with the Workshop's
    service salt followed by the username, as the Workshop frontend does.
  req F-1.3: The token's `AccessToken.source` is the deployment's hostname, so the connection
    itself says which deployment it signs in to.
  req F-1.4: Testing the connection authenticates the stored token; a rejected token fails with
    `ConnectionTestError`.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Bind a workspace to the space

  req F-2.1: The connection's sync targets are the account's workspaces, newest first, after a
    "New workspace" target.
  req F-2.2: Binding a workspace finds or creates the space's `Workspace` for that workspace id;
    binding "New workspace" first creates and titles a workspace on the deployment.
  req F-2.3: Syncing the connection refreshes the name and gadget list of every `Workspace` it
    binds.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Run gadgets in the workspace article

  req F-3.1: The article lists the workspace's gadgets live, as the deployment reports them, and
    marks a gadget that only exists in a chat's proposed changes.
  req F-3.2: The picked gadget's UI runs in a frame with a null origin, sandboxed to scripts and
    user-opened popups, under a policy that forbids every network request.
  req F-3.3: The frame's only connection is the `MessagePort` the gadget posts on start, which the
    plugin bridges to the gadget's server through `connectToGadget`.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Chat with the workspace agent

  req F-4.1: The workspace agent is offered in every chat's agent picker, beside Composer's own
    agent and Claude Code, and runs in the workspace bound to the chat's space.
  req F-4.2: A chat's first turn starts a workspace chat; the chat records its id as a foreign key
    (source `cloudflare-os-chat`) and every later turn continues that workspace chat.
  req F-4.3: The agent's messages are added to the chat as they complete: its reasoning, a line per
    tool call, and its text.
  req F-4.4: When a turn ends with proposed gadget changes, the chat asks to accept them
    (`mergeChanges`) or revert them (`revertChanges`).
  req F-4.5: When a turn ends with gatekeeper actions pending, the chat asks to approve or reject
    each one, previewing what it would do.
  req F-4.6: A turn that is cancelled or runs out of time stops the workspace agent.
  req F-4.7: A space with no bound workspace fails the turn with a message that says to connect
    Cloudflare OS and bind a workspace.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Request ids round-trip
  given: a merge request for chat 3 and an action request for action 12
  then: decoding each request id returns its target; an id another agent issued decodes to nothing
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Agent messages become blocks
  given: an agent message with reasoning, two tool calls (one failed) and text
  then: it becomes a reasoning block, one text block listing both tool calls, and its text, in that order
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: The gadget page has no network
  given: a gadget's UI code
  then: the page's policy sets `connect-src 'none'`, and the gadget code runs after the prelude that opens the port
```

## QA

Executable tests against a running Composer and a live Cloudflare OS deployment. The account must
already exist on the deployment: signups are closed there, so a test cannot create one.

```mdl
test QA-1: Connect, bind a workspace, and build a gadget with the Cloudflare OS agent
  desc: |
    The primary journey: sign in from the connector form, bind a new workspace to the space, ask the
    workspace agent for a gadget from a Composer chat, accept its change, and use the gadget in the article.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.3, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3, F-4.1, F-4.2, F-4.3, F-4.4]
  status: passing            # 2026-11-02; recorded by the autocue flow build-a-gadget against cloudflareos.dxos.network
  given:
    - an identity exists and a space is open
    - plugin-cloudflare-os is enabled
    - account: a password account on https://cloudflareos.dxos.network
    - no Cloudflare OS connection exists in the space
  steps:
    - name: Open the space's connections
      do: In the navtree, expand the space's Settings and click Connections.
      expect: the Connections article shows "Add connection" with a Connect button
    - name: Pick Cloudflare OS
      do: Click Connect, choose Cloudflare OS and click Continue.
      expect: a form asks for the deployment (filled with https://cloudflareos.dxos.network), a username and a password
    - name: Sign in
      do: Enter the account's username and password and click Save.
      expect: |
        the connection opens as "Cloudflare OS · <username>", its details name the deployment and the
        account, and a target picker lists "New workspace" first, then the account's workspaces
      note: The password is never stored; the connection holds the session token login() returned.
    - name: Bind a new workspace
      do: Choose "New workspace" and click Save.
      expect: a "Cloudflare OS workspaces" section appears under the space's content, holding one workspace named "Composer"
    - name: Open the workspace
      do: Click the workspace in the navtree.
      expect: its article opens and says the workspace has no gadgets yet
    - name: Pick the Cloudflare OS agent
      do: Open the Assistant companion, open the agent picker and choose Cloudflare OS.
      expect: the picker lists Cloudflare OS beside Composer, and the prompt shows Cloudflare OS as the agent
    - name: Ask for a gadget
      do: Ask "Build a tally counter gadget that shows the count, with - and + buttons." and send it.
      expect: |
        the agent's reasoning, a line per tool call (createGadget, writeFile) and its reply appear in the
        chat; the article lists the new gadget marked "(proposed)"; the turn ends with "Accept changes to
        <gadget>?"
      note: |
        The agent is a model; its words, gadget title and code vary from run to run. A run once built a
        gadget that passed a plain class to `gadget.subscribe()` and never showed its count, which is why
        the prompt asks for the count to be shown.
    - name: Accept the change
      do: Click "Accept changes".
      expect: the card reads "Answered: Accept changes", and the gadget's tab loses "(proposed)"
    - name: Run the gadget
      do: Click the gadget's tab, then click + in the gadget three times.
      expect: the gadget runs in the article and its count reads 3
      note: Each click crosses the sandbox's port to Composer and the WebSocket to the gadget's server.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Composer is the frontend and a Cloudflare OS deployment is the backend for a space, built as a Composer plugin.
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A Cloudflare OS workspace maps one-to-one to a Composer space.
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Workspace, F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The Cloudflare OS agent is a third kind of chat agent, beside Composer's assistant and Claude.
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Authentication to Cloudflare OS goes through Composer connectors.
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: For the prototype, the deployment's authentication may be loosened to make the integration work.
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The connector signs in with the deployment's own password login and stores the session token, with the deployment hostname as its source. Fills in [D-4] and [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3]
  why: A browser cannot set Cloudflare Access headers on a WebSocket, and with Access on the Workshop refuses `/api` from any other origin; password sign-in authenticates in-band and accepts any origin.
  rejected: Access service tokens, which a browser cannot send on a WebSocket; relaying the WebSocket through EDGE, which needs an EDGE change.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A space binds its workspace as the connection's sync target, with a "New workspace" target that creates one. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
  why: The connector framework's target picker already asks which remote object a space binds, so the one-to-one binding needs no UI of its own.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Proposed gadget changes and pending gatekeeper actions become request blocks in the chat. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.4, F-4.5]
  why: Composer already renders request blocks as approval cards and routes the answer to the agent's `respond`, which maps onto `mergeChanges`, `revertChanges`, `approveAction` and `rejectAction`.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Gadgets run in a frame that reproduces the Workshop's sandbox. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.2, F-3.3]
  why: A gadget's security rests on its frame having no network and only the port to its server; a looser frame in Composer would undo it.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: A turn follows the workspace chat by polling with one-request HTTP batches, and the workspace article reopens its live session when it drops. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.3, F-3.1]
  why: A live WebSocket subscription that drops ends silently, which left a turn waiting after the agent had finished; a request has no connection to lose.
  rejected: Reconnecting the turn's subscription and replaying from the last sequence, which needs the same end-of-turn detection polling gives directly.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The QA prompt asks for a gadget "that shows the count". Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-02
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [QA-1]
  why: Without it the agent once built a counter whose display never received the count, so the test could not judge the run step.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A cancelled or timed-out turn stops the workspace agent. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-4.6]
  why: Otherwise the agent keeps running on the deployment after Composer stops following it, and can queue gated actions nobody is watching for.
```
